# 지호: a school kid. Talks to everyone without 요 (반말), which from a kid is cheeky, not rude.
# (format: js/core/villagers.js)

=== person jiho
at afternoon golmok 50 62
at evening jeong 62 68
greet jh_hi
chat 0 jh_what
chat 0 jh_homework
bye jh_bye

=== scene jh_hi
jiho[happy]: {안녕}!
(A kid with a school bag as big as he is. No 요 anywhere: he talks to you like you're in his class.)

=== scene jh_what
jiho: {뭐} {해}?
(He tries to read your notebook upside down.)
* {탈}{을|을/를} {찾아요}. -> jh_what_a
* {몰라요}. -> jh_what_b

=== scene jh_what_a
jiho[surprised]: {탈}? {진짜}?
(His eyes go wide.)
jiho[happy]: {좋아}! {같이} {가}!
(He marches off three steps, realizes he has no idea where, and comes back.)
! rel jiho +1

=== scene jh_what_b
jiho[happy]: {몰라}? 하하. {나}{도} {몰라}.
(He shrugs with his whole body.)

=== scene jh_homework
jiho[sad]: {숙제} {싫어}.
(He gives his school bag a small kick.)
* {저}{도} {싫어요}. -> jh_homework_a
* {숙제} {좋아요}! -> jh_homework_b

=== scene jh_homework_a
jiho[happy]: 하하! {좋아}!
(At last, an adult who understands.)
! rel jiho +1

=== scene jh_homework_b
jiho[surprised]: {진짜}...?
(He looks at you the way you would look at someone who likes the dentist.)

=== scene jh_bye
jiho: {안녕}!
(He is gone before you can answer.)
